  <title>REMOVE TABLE Command</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>Databases</keyword>
    <keyword>REMOVE TABLE command</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">REMOVE TABLE Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Removes a table from the current database. The table becomes a free table, or is deleted from disk.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">REMOVE TABLE &lt;TableName&gt; [DELETE | RECYCLE]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">&lt;TableName&gt;<tab />The name of the table in the current database.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">DELETE<tab />Deletes the table file (and its memo and index files) from disk after it has been removed from the database.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">RECYCLE<tab />Intended to move the files to the Recycle Bin. At this moment the files are deleted permanently, just like with the DELETE clause. <text styleclass="Body Text" style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;">RECYCLE IS NOT FULLY SUPPORTED AT THIS MOMENT</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Without the DELETE and RECYCLE clauses the table file remains on disk as a free table.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_ADD_TABLE">ADD TABLE</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_RENAME_TABLE">RENAME TABLE</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_DELETE_DATABASE">DELETE DATABASE</link></para>
  </body>
